{
  "prompt": "3D diagram of a Whirlygig mechanism: a small sphere inside a torus, with two Lissajous curves drawn on the sphere's hemispheres. Show rotation axes, pins, and coupling that map the sphere rotation to the torus surface. Include labeled axes (X, Y, Z), the torus major radius R, sphere radius r_s, and the composite trajectory in red. Depict latitude and longitude angles θ(t) and φ(t), with light shading on the torus and sphere to indicate depth. Illustrate mechanical pins connecting rotations to the trajectory.",
  "size": "1024x1024",
  "n": 1
}

{
  "prompt": "Visualize the Whirligig soliton landscape for 3-body candidate solutions. Show: a central 2-body seed orbit in 3D space, branching perturbations as slightly offset paths, with small arrows indicating δv perturbations. Overlay 4D Lissajous projections as semi-transparent colored curves, with clusters labeled A, B, C. Make it clear that viable trajectories are highlighted and duplicates are collapsed into clusters. Artistic but scientifically suggestive, not abstract.",
  "size": "1024x1024"
}

{
  "prompt": "A schematic 3D visualization of a He3-inspired filament soliton. The filament curves in 3D space (x, y, z) as a helix with twists and loops. Color along the filament encodes the 4th dimension (torsion phase or Zottenwelt backpull). The filament should show regions of higher 'pseudo-mass' as thicker segments, with smooth quasi-periodic variation. Background neutral, scientific schematic style.",
  "size": "1024x1024"
}
